          "vulnSlug": "other-resource-exhaustion",
          "title": "Browser capture ignores byte limits and buffers output in memory",
          "description": "`mediaInput` accepts `maxBytes`, but the limit is only passed to `downloadToFile` for `action === 'download'`. For `screenshot` and `pdf`, the workflow calls `browserCapture` without the limit; `browserCapture` runs `agent-browser` against the user-controlled URL and destination, then reads the entire generated file with `Bun.file(dest).arrayBuffer()` just to count bytes. A hostile page rendered as PDF, or another very large capture, can force the CLI or an automation worker to write a large file and then allocate the full file in memory even when `--max-bytes` was supplied.",
